Hi Vinoth,

Currently, return requests are not linked to a specific device, but only to an expected equipment category.

For mobile phones, there is no distinction between Samsung, Android, Apple, etc. All of them belong to the same “Mobile Phone” category.

In your example, if a visitor returns two mobile phones:

* The first phone will be associated with the existing open return request.
* For the second phone, the application will automatically create an additional equipment return request.

This ensures that both returned devices are properly recorded and allows AM/HM to be updated accordingly.

So, there is no need to identify or match a specific device with the existing RITM.
